Application Behavior – Netflix Button Flow
	1.	When the user clicks the Netflix button, the application checks whether the Netflix app is installed on the TV.
	2.		•	If Netflix is already installed, it launches the app directly.
	•	If Netflix is not installed, a dialog box appears prompting the user to initialize the token and proceed with the installation.
	3.	After successful installation, the user can either launch Netflix from the dialog box or, in future sessions, by simply clicking the Netflix button.
	4.	With this update, Netflix will be installed only once. Going forward, the application will detect its presence and launch it directly, without showing the dialog box again.
